# No collateral damage

When you change HUD, pit, colors, tools, or sounds, treat nearby layout as in-scope. A change is not done if it overlaps, clips, or hides something that was already working.

- Dig chrome (Tools, wallet, clock, Menu, End shift, Finds) must stay off the **whole dig-site hole**, not just the cell grid. The hole includes west/east/north pads (`chunk_pad`). Measure against that cutout.
- Do not grow one section by covering another. If Tools needs width, move the pit or shrink the empty gutter — never paint over dirt cells.
- After the edit, check the neighbors you touched: left rail vs pit, header vs pit, Finds vs pit, clock vs wallet.
- Run the related Godot suites (`test_hud_layout`, plus any suite for the behavior you changed) and fix new failures before you stop.

```
# BAD — Tools frame ends on the cell grid, so the west pad sits under the panel
frame_right <= pit.position.x

# GOOD — Tools frame clears the hole, including the west pad
frame_right <= pit.position.x - chunk_pad - gap
```
